# Lick: Slides (repertoire plan: st-lick-slide). An original 8-bar lick in A minor pentatonic
# over an Am7 groove, built around three slides, all with finger 3:
#   bar 1:     string 3 fret 7 (D) up to fret 9 (E): out of box 1 into box 2 (finger 1 now on fret 7);
#   bar 3:     string 2 fret 8 (G) up to fret 10 (A): finger 3 plays the G so it can slide
#              (finger 1 lands on fret 8, beside C at string 1 fret 8);
#   bars 5-6:  the long shift on string 4 from fret 5 (G) to fret 10 (C), across the bar line.
# Bar 7 slides back down string 3 from fret 9 to fret 7, which puts the hand home in box 1.
# The hand moves back down to box 1 during the rests at the ends of bars 2 and 4.
# Phrases 1 and 3 ask (they stop on E and G), phrases 2 and 4 answer (they come home to A).
title: Lick: Slides
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original lick in A minor pentatonic
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
tags: slide, position shift, minor pentatonic, lick
tempo: 92
time: 4/4
key: Am

